sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch12-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Although terrestrial mammals are absent from oceanic islands, bats occur on almost every island, and remote islands often have their own endemic bat species, because bats can fly across wide spaces of sea and are then modified in their new homes.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bats occur on almost every island, often as endemic species";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XII, “Geographical Distribution, continued”; section “Absence of Batrachians and of terrestrial Mammals”. Scope: bats on oceanic islands"
}
